  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "HQczNFa8akf653mxKL8CIEpC+hY=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:26.302Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Accenture is present in the Flowable Partner Finder and marked do-not-pitch, labelled as enterprise anti-persona AP-2 at 513,000 staff. The wording of the flag is precise and worth preserving: there is \"no procurement-track motion in this brief\".\n\nThat locates the missing piece in Powerhouse's own approach rather than in Accenture. The exclusion is not a claim that a firm of this size could never adopt the stack; it is a claim that the brief has no play for a buyer who can only be reached through enterprise procurement. Read that way, the exclusion is a scoping decision with an expiry condition \u2014 it would need revisiting if a procurement-led motion were ever built.\n\nThe same exclusion catches the other largest names in the sweep: Tata Consultancy Services at 600,000+ staff and EPAM on non-EU enterprise scale. Since those are also the firms carrying the highest partner tiers, the practical lesson is that presence in a vendor's partner directory is not a qualification signal at the top end of the market.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Accenture (IE Dublin / global) \u2014 accenture.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> 513,000 staff. Enterprise anti-persona (AP-2) \u2014 no procurement-track motion in this brief \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:26.302050Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:26.302054Z"
    }
  },
